ChatGPT Wants to Read Health Records
​OpenAI wants ChatGPT to help people with health questions.
​To do this better, the AI may need access to health records.
​Health records contain information about a person's medical history, medicines, and test results.
​OpenAI says this could help ChatGPT give more useful answers.
​However, ChatGPT is not a doctor.
​People should not use it instead of a real medical professional.
​Some people are worried about privacy.
​They want to know how their personal health information will be protected.
​Experts say strong security is very important.
​AI can help people understand health information.
​But important medical decisions should always be made with a doctor.
